    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#967;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Magnetic field inside the material in solenoid is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>'</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&#967;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></math>, here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi></math>&nbsp;is current.</p><p>Now, magnetic field with air as medium&nbsp;inside solenoid is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></math>.</p><p>So, fractional increase is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>'</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>&#967;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
